From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:14:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vbscript: Complete the error string table, and translate it
 as Windows does.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Err.Raise and VBScript's own errors look their description up in
vbscript.dll's string table by number. Windows 11 (build 29671) has 130
strings there; the table had 88. The rest are added: file and device
errors, Automation and safety errors, "An exception occurred", the
compilation errors 1001, 1003, 1023, 1027, 1034, 1043 and 1056, the
regular expression errors 5016 to 5021, and True, False, OK, Cancel,
Help and the element, calendar and blocked-script messages. Only 30000,
whose English text could not be checked, is left out.

The Chinese translation is Windows' own, read from its vbscript.dll and
jscript.dll string tables, which agree where the two engines share a
string. vbscript's "File not found" is translated apart from comdlg32's
("找不到文件" there), and its True and False apart from oleaut32's; the
other languages keep their translation of "File not found".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 33bb49863631da9c4d51e0be0836ee440c411445)

